In the beginning, there was only silence and stars. The world had not yet turned, the wind had not yet whispered, 
and time itself was still catching its breath. Then came the spark—the first flicker of life that danced across 
the void like a whisper in the dark. From this moment, everything began: oceans churned, mountains rose, forests 
spread their green banners beneath the sky, and creatures of every shape and sound began to move, to speak, to sing.
The eagle flies not just to hunt, but to understand the wind. The river flows not merely to reach the sea, but to 
remember every stone it touches. Beneath the canopy of ancient trees, forgotten languages echo in the rustle of leaves, 
and the moon, full and patient, listens to the dreams of wolves. Operation Silent Storm begins at the stroke of midnight. 
Units Alpha through Echo are to proceed to the designated coordinates with stealth and precision. Communication is to be 
maintained using encrypted channels only. Contingency plans Charlie and Delta are on standby should the primary objective 
encounter unexpected resistance. You are the keeper of this message. Guard it well, for it carries more than just words—it 
holds the weight of intention, the burden of truth, and the shadow of secrets not meant for the careless. Trust no one outside 
the circle. Repeat: trust no one. This is not just a story. It is a signal. A pulse in the static. A path through the noise.